# Project-local .vercelignore for the contexia-wizard Vercel project.
# Vercel looks for .vercelignore inside the project's Root Directory setting
# (contexia-wizard) -- without this file it fell back to the repo-root
# .vercelignore, which deliberately excludes contexia-wizard/ (to keep its
# source/node_modules out of the contexia-web-app static deploy), stripping
# this entire folder before the build even started. NEXT_NO_VERSION on every
# deploy since that repo-root rule was added.
#
# Do NOT add .next/ or .vercel/ here: Vercel's own Next.js build writes its
# output into .next/ during the build step and needs it to still be visible
# afterward to package the deployment (routes-manifest.json lives there).
# Ignoring .next/ made the build succeed but then fail to find its own
# output -- confirmed live 2026-09-23.
node_modules/
*.log
# NOT .env.local / .env.*.local: the CI workflow's `vercel pull` writes
# .env.production.local here, and the Next.js output tracer bundles it as a
# traced file for the serverless functions -- excluding it here made
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt` fail with ENOENT on a dangling readlink.
# Confirmed live 2026-09-26.
